 from every vertex over the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reduced weights h(u) + w - h(v), which are nonnegative. Parallel edges count by their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cheapest. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"findNegativeCycle(weight:)"},{"text":" gives a negative cycle when this is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":". On sparse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graphs this is faster than ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"floydWarshallShortestPaths(weight:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(nm) for Bellman–Ford in the worst case (about one pass when no weight is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"negative), then O(n · (n + m) log n); O(n²) space."}]}]},{"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No weight is NaN; every sum fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":", the reduced weights and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reduced distances included. With floating point, distances are converted back from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reduced ones and can differ from Floyd–Warshall’s by rounding."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Shortest paths between every ordered pair of vertices by Johnson’s algorithm, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the graph has a negative cycle anywhere (a negative loop counts)."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/johnsonShortestPaths(weight:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"